\title{Countability Axioms}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    A topological space #{X} is \strong{first-countable} if every point
    #{x\in X} has an at most countable [local basis](def-005L). It is
    \strong{second-countable} if its topology has an at most countable
    [basis](def-005M).
}
\p{
    These conditions constrain two different scales. First-countability gives
    a countable collection of tests near each individual point, while
    second-countability gives one countable collection of basic open sets for
    the whole space.
}
